BELANGER III -Hea-Gno-Mal-Neu ascended to demigod-hood, 4719992
points.

I have been up all night playing Nethack, and am a little bit drowsy,
so I'll keep this brief:

There was an altar on dlvl1, so I converted it and made some holy
water, then boosted my hitpoints with potions of extra healing.  Then
I did the protection racket, picking up a BoH in Minetown, and some
early Identify and Magic Missile spellbooks somewhere in the Mines.
Went on to Sokoban, got the "oRefl, then went back up and finished
Minesend.  Picked up a tinning kit somewhere along the way, and
started catching giants and tengus.

No wishes yet, but potions of healing were smoky, so things were
looking all right.  I cleared out each level in the main dungeon,
eventually reaching Fort Ludios.

Thisl was my first time there, and it was a little disappointing-- no
useful items, no wishes from the throne, just lots and lots of gold.
As rich as the late Croesus, I went back to minetown and traded it all
for some more protection.  Then I converted the altar, executed the
(cross-aligned) priest, and camped a while with my spellbook of Create
Monster.  Quickly got bored with this, but managed a couple of golden,
a protection point or two, and Stealth intrinsic.

Hauled the 80 000-or-so zorkmids up to dlvl1 to await my departure,
then headed down to the Quest.  By now I had about 6 blessed tins of
tengu, so I ate them and got the desired results.  The Quest itself
was typical, and I was out of there soon enough.

Down to Medusa, then to the Castle.  Went in the Castle's back door,
found a T-shirt and some Gauntlets of Dexterity; fought my way to the
Wand, which I used for the Eye of the Aethiopica, a bunch of magic
markers, some speed boots, and, just before entering the Planes, a
blessed Archon figurine.

Continued on down into Gehennom.  Not all that eventful; Juiblex had
been summoned and dispatched early (by an angry Minetown water
daemon), and I bribed Baalzebub for 400 gold pieces.  For once,
Minetown had an adequate number of candles, so there was no real
trouble when I reached the bottom.

I used teleportitis to my advantage while escaping Gehennom, since I
kept getting thrown back to random places in the maze, and eventually
I even made it out!  Then began a steady journey upward.

About dlvl15, I noticed that I was starting to get hungry.  Without
bothering to consult a wand of enlightenment, I tried to pray for
food.  Hermes, displeased, revoked roughly 20 points in protection.

This was when the neighbours heard me swearing at the monitor.

This was also when I panicked, and--forfeiting any trace of style--
started polypiling amulets.  The fact that none of the new amulets was
destroyed to save my life hardly counts to lessen my transgression.
Mea culpa.  Two hundred and fifty-five rosaries coming up.  (I got a
bunch of cheap amulets of strangulation at the dollar store, and I'm
warming up the wand)

After that shameful event, I proceeded as planned.  All the way up to
dlvl1, where I collected Croesus' legacy, and to the up-stair.  The
up-stair.  What was that beside the up-stair?

An Archon was beside the up-stair.  An angry Archon.  Through some
skillful ^T -ing, however, I had soon left him behind, and was on my
way through the Planes.

I found a Crystal Ball on Earth, and used it to find the portals.  The
elemental Planes ere uneventful, mostly because, still freaked out
about my AC, I ran straight through them.

When I arrived on the Astral Plane, I got my usual Guardian Angel, and
then supplemented it with the aforementioned Blessed Archon Figurine.
While those two tore up some priests, I went to each of the chamber
doors and cast Wizard Lock.

"That should hold those darn Riders," thought I.  I was just debating
which door to try first, when something purple appeared to my left.
Purple and ampersandy.  This being Death, and me not wanting to deal
with him at that particular moment, I ran to the right, finding
another open door, and Pestilence threading his way between my pets.
He ate Wand of Death, and I stepped over his body and into his room.

I locked the door behind me again, this time not actually expecting it
to hold, and blew my recently-found Magic Whistle.  My pets made short
work of everyone there, and then in the next room.  I ran to the High
Altar and found, to my delight, that it was co-aligned--a good thing,
too, since ALL THREE Riders were not five steps behind me at the time.

That's all that I can remember right now.  I'd post pages and pages of
inventory and stuff, but I didn't think to copy that text, and I'm not
going to transcribe the screenshots right now.

